The code itself is valid Node.js/CommonJS syntax, but the problem is where you're using it.

const { send } = require("vite");

require() is normally available in Node.js, but your login JavaScript is running in the browser through Vite. The browser doesn't have a require function, so you get:

require is not defined

Also, you almost certainly don't need this line at all for the code you've shown.

