Why it seems like the code is "correct"

This:

const { send } = require("vite");

isn't necessarily syntactically wrong. The issue is that require() belongs to a Node/CommonJS environment.

For example, this can work in a Node file:

const something = require("something");

But when Vite sends your frontend JavaScript to the browser, the browser sees:

require(...)

and says:

ReferenceError: require is not defined

Vite itself uses Node internally, but your frontend code isn't running inside Node.

Also, vite doesn't provide some send function that you need for your fetch() calls. For your account code, you can simply use:

fetch(...)

So in your case: delete that line.

