Then your frontend:

fetch("https://easy-animals.onrender.com/allAccounts")

matches it.

2. You forgot await in createAccount

You have:

const response = fetch("https://easy-animals.onrender.com/addUser", {

It needs to be:

const response = await fetch("https://easy-animals.onrender.com/addUser", {

Without await, response is a Promise rather than the actual response.

So this:

if (!response.ok)

won't work correctly.

3. Your Sign In event listener is in the wrong place

You currently have this inside getDataAccounts():

document.querySelector(".signIn").addEventListener("click", function () {
    getDataAccounts();
});

That's a problem because the listener only gets added after getDataAccounts() has already been called.

Move it outside:

document.querySelector(".signIn").addEventListener("click", function () {
    getDataAccounts();
});

Put it near the top of your JS.

